entries.text:
A one-take FPV drone first-person-view video, a 33-second continuous long take, no cuts, no jump cuts, no transitions. The shot starts inside high-altitude clouds, descending along a continuous flight line through cloud layers, mist, light and shadow, a valley, a waterfall, a lake surface, a flower field, city buildings, and a near-ground plaza. Throughout, 11 distinct independent language display zones appear in sequence, each zone showing only the corresponding single language's text, no mixing, no overlay, no adding other languages.
0-3s, [reference image 1] cloud masses naturally form the Chinese "你好";
3-6s, [reference image 2] thin mist and volumetric light form the English "Hello";
6-9s, [reference image 3] high-altitude water vapor and sunlight projection form the Spanish (Mexico) "Hola";
9-12s, [reference image 4] airborne ribbons form the Indonesian "Halo";
12-15s, [reference image 5] a kite formation forms the Malay "Hai";
15-18s, [reference image 6] valley morning mist forms the Thai "สวัสดี";
18-21s, [reference image 7] waterfall spray forms the Arabic "مرحبا";
21-24s, [reference image 8] the lake's reflection and ripple light patterns form the Portuguese "Olá";
24-27s, [reference image 9] a flower field and grassland naturally arrange into the Vietnamese "Xin chào";
27-30s, [reference image 10] the reflected light and shadow on city glass buildings form the Japanese "こんにちは";
30-33s, [reference image 11] the fountain spray, ground paving, and light strips of the near-ground plaza form the Korean "안녕하세요".
The overall atmosphere is an early-morning sunrise, golden backlight, soft volumetric light, realistic clouds and mist, natural motion blur, cinematic realism. The camera speed starts slowly at 3-5 m/s, gradually accelerating to 14-16 m/s crossing the natural landscape, then decelerating to 2-3 m/s to hover stably at the near-ground plaza. Camera parameters: wide-angle lens, 24fps, smooth FPV drone movement, pitch transitioning gradually from -5° to -18°, finally returning to 0°; slight yaw ±10°, roll kept within 0-10°, ensuring a continuous, stable, realistic one-take flight feel.
